   "description": "<p>The Alexandria Jazz Festival returns for its 48th edition, bringing together some of the best artists in the area for an afternoon and evening of Black American Music. Vendors will offer food and drinks, while the festival setup will include games and art projects.</p>\n<p><strong>1 p.m. &#8211; Silver Tones &#8211; </strong>The Silver Tones is a Northern Virginia-based swing band led by trumpeter and vocalist Wendy Marie.</p>\n<p><strong>2:30 p.m. &#8211; Irish Breakfast Band &#8211; </strong>The Irish Breakfast band is a collective of DMV-based musicians who perform a repertoire of Celtic music.</p>\n<p><strong>3:45 p.m. &#8211; Decades Band &#8211; </strong>The Decades band performs a mixture of smooth jazz and R&amp;B.</p>\n<p><strong>5 p.m. &#8211; Jason Masi &#8211; </strong>Singer-songwriter Jason Masi draws influence from classic soul, blues and acoustic rock.</p>\n",
