   "description": "<p>The Alexandria Jazz Festival returns for its 48th edition, bringing together some of the best artists in the area for an afternoon and evening of Black American Music and poetry. Vendors will offer food and drinks, while the festival setup will include games and art projects.</p>\n<p><strong>12:15 p.m. &#8211; Eric Byrd &#8211; </strong>Vocalist and pianist Eric Byrd sings in a silky croon that’s not too far from Nat “King” Cole – but with more soul and gospel influence.</p>\n<p><strong>1:30 p.m. &#8211; Alex Parchment &#8211; </strong>D.C.-based trumpeter Alex Parchment performs a blend of soul, funk, hip-hop and jazz.</p>\n<p><strong>2:45 p.m. &#8211; Improviso Jazz </strong></p>\n<p><strong>4:20 &#8211; Michael Hawkins and the Brotherhood &#8211; </strong>Bassist Michael Hawkins leads his ensemble of Richmond-based musicians through selections of straight-ahead jazz.</p>\n<p><strong>5:50 &#8211; Poetry by Prophecy Poet </strong></p>\n<p><strong>5:55 &#8211; Kayazhanna &#8211; </strong> Kayazhanna is a young singer-songwriter in the D.C. area.</p>\n<p><strong>7:25 &#8211; Alexandria Poet Laureate and ACPS Student Poetry </strong></p>\n<p><strong>7:35 &#8211; Madz Johnson &#8211; </strong>Singer-songwriter Madz Johnson pulls influence from funk, soul and jazz.</p>\n",
