   "description": "<p>The Alexandria Jazz Festival returns for its 48th edition, bringing together some of the best artists in the area for an afternoon and evening of Black American Music. Vendors will offer food and drinks, while the festival setup will include games and art projects.</p>\n<p><strong>12:15 p.m. &#8211; Jordan Curls &#8211; </strong>Singer-songwriter Jordan Curls blends jazz, neo-soul, hip-hop and spoken word.</p>\n<p><strong>1:30 p.m. &#8211; DJ One Luv &#8211; </strong>DJ One Luv performs a wide range of Black music, including jazz, R&amp;B, Caribbean, afrobeat, house, hip-hop, Latin, rock and Motown classics. Two separate sets at 1:30 and 4:15 p.m.</p>\n<p><strong>2:45 p.m. &#8211; Orquesta Manplesa &#8211; </strong>Salsa band Orquesta Manplesa pays homage to D.C.&#8217;s Latin musical traditions, blending traditional and contemporary sounds.</p>\n<p><strong>5:10 &#8211; Future Band &#8211; </strong>The Roots-influenced FutureBandDC fuses elements of hip-hop, soul and go-go.</p>\n",
